.\" Manpage for tilemaker.
.TH man 1 "19 Oct 2026" "1.0" "tilemaker man page"
.SH NAME
tilemaker \- Renders the vector tiles of an area from its OpenStreetMap data
.SH SYNOPSIS
tilemaker --input area.osm --output area.mbtiles
.br
tilemaker --db --bbox minlon,minlat,maxlon,maxlat --output area.mbtiles
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents briefly the
.B tilemaker
command of tilemaker-core.
.PP
.B tilemaker
renders the vector tiles of a small area, from zoom 11 up, from the
OpenStreetMap data of that area: a file, or a pycrocosm map database. It
uses the schema of OpenMapTiles by default, but custom vector tiles can be
produced by modifying the JSON config (layer config and general options)
and Lua processing script (mapping OSM tags to vector tile layers/attributes).
.PP
This program follows the usual GNU command line syntax, with long
options starting with two dashes (`-').
A summary of options is included below:
.TP
\fB\-\-input
Source file covering the area (.osm, .o5m, .pbf or .json). May be given
more than once.
.TP
\fB\-\-db
Read from a pycrocosm map database. Takes an optional libpq connection
string; without one, the PG* environment variables are used. Needs \-\-bbox.
.TP
\fB\-\-table\-prefix
The map database's static tables, the imported planet (planet_static_ if
not specified). Empty to read the modify tables' views alone.
.TP
\fB\-\-modify\-prefix
The map database's modify tables, the edits over the static ones
(pycrocosm_mod_ if not specified).
.TP
\fB\-\-output
Target path for vector tiles. Specify .mbtiles/.sqlite to create
an mbtiles archive, .pmtiles to create a PMTiles archive, or a directory
to create individual .mvt files.
.TP
\fB\-\-config
Path to layer and global config file (.json). config.json assumed if
not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-process
Path to Lua processing script for processing tags. process.lua assumed if
not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-merge
Merge with existing .mbtiles/.sqlite file.
.TP
\fB\-\-tile
Render just this tile, given as z/x/y, reading the tile and a margin around
it. Write it to a directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-bbox
The area to render (as minlon,minlat,maxlon,maxlat). Needed with \-\-db;
otherwise the bounds the input declares, or of its nodes, are used.
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-integrity
Use ways that are missing some of their nodes, rather than skipping them.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose
Outputs any issues encountered during tile creation.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet
Suppress standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-tile\-timings
Log how long each tile takes.
.TP
\fB\-\-threads
Number of threads (automatically detected if 0).
.TP
\fB\-\-help
Show help message for tilemaker.
.PP
.SH AUTHOR
This manual page was written by tilemaker contributors.
